  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Health Systems capacity to provide equitable, effective and efficient package of comprehensive and quality health services to Ethiopian people. - Ethiopia (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia, RSSH, Federal Ministry of Health of the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia (FMOH)This program has the following goals: Reduce maternal mortality mortality to less than 200 per 100,000 live births from the baseline of 2013.  Reduce morbidity and mortality due to HIV, TB and malaria.  Reduce neonatal mortality to less than 15 per 1000 live births by 2020 from the baseline of 2013.  Reduce under five mortality mortality to less than 35 per 1000 live births by 2020 from baseline of 2013. The objectives of this program are: Improve district management capacity.  Improve financial resources management and financial reporting at all levels.  Improve human resource capacity that enhance community and health information system.  Improve service delivery through strengthening the laboratory services.  Strengthen national health management information system.  Strengthen pharmaceuticals supply chain management system</narrative>
  </description>
